# Vercel deployment ignore list — the counterpart to `exclude:` in _config.yml.
#
# Jekyll's exclude list is a GitHub Pages mechanism and does NOTHING on Vercel:
# Vercel uploads and serves whatever is in the deployed directory. This file is
# what keeps a path in the repo without putting it on the web here. Anything
# added to one list almost always belongs in the other too — keep them in sync.
#
# NOTE (2026-08): the live website is the React app in `neurole-react/`, which
# is deployed as its OWN Vercel project (framework "vite", output `dist/`). This
# root-level Vercel config and these exclude lists only matter if a site is ever
# (re)deployed straight from the repo root. The React project has its own
# vercel.json and ignore handling — none of this applies to it.
#
# Nothing is deleted; removing a line republishes the path.

# --- Non-deployed assets ---------------------------------------------------
# The designated archive/dump folder: every image, spreadsheet and zip. Stays
# out of the repo-root deployment. (The React app copies the images it needs
# into its own public/ folder, so nothing served needs this.) The duplicate
# whole-site copy that used to need an entry here was deleted outright instead.
assets/
# All question banks live under assets/ now (not the root), answers included.
# The live games read the published Google Sheet CSV, so nothing fetches these.
*.xlsx

# --- Source archives -------------------------------------------------------
# Old whole-site snapshot zips and the daily/neuroanatomy game source zips.
# Kept for history under assets/; nothing on a deployed site links to them.
*.zip

# --- React app -------------------------------------------------------------
# The actual website: source, not build output. Deployed as its own Vercel
# project. Serving this from the root would expose the whole codebase.
neurole-react/

# --- Not part of the website -----------------------------------------------
# Cloudflare Worker source; lives at neurole-react/scripts/ai-worker.js and
# runs on Cloudflare, never fetched by a browser.
wrangler.jsonc
# Tooling and docs.
package.json
package-lock.json
# Every markdown file in the root is a note or a readme for whoever is working
# on the repo — none is a page. Named by pattern so a new one does not silently
# become a URL. (Article content lives in the excluded neurole-react/.)
*.md

# --- Other platforms' config -----------------------------------------------
# Both would otherwise be served as plain static files from the site root.
# CNAME is a GitHub Pages convention; on Vercel the domain is set in project
# settings, so it is meaningless here — but harmless to keep in the repo.
_config.yml
CNAME

# --- Dotfiles --------------------------------------------------------------
# Jekyll ignores these automatically; Vercel does not, so they need naming
# here or they end up served from the site root.
.gitignore
.vercelignore